WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.900
Desktop: Okilum Sync keeps your notes on two computers, directly between them. No account, no cloud service.

2
00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:12.980
Desktop: On the computer that has your notes, open the menu and choose Share with another computer.

3
00:00:13.130 --> 00:00:15.980
Desktop: Give this computer a name.

4
00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:21.320
Desktop: Next to your vault, choose Share with my computers. Your files stay where they are.

5
00:00:21.470 --> 00:00:28.700
Desktop: Then choose Add computer. Okilum shows a one-time pairing link. Copy it to your other computer.

6
00:00:28.850 --> 00:00:36.730
Laptop: On the new computer, install the Okilum beta. On the welcome screen, choose Get notes from another computer.

7
00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.770
Laptop: Name this computer, paste the link, and choose Connect.

8
00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:46.110
Desktop: Back on the first computer, check that the name is right, and confirm it.

9
00:00:46.260 --> 00:00:49.730
Laptop: The new computer now lists the vaults you shared.

10
00:00:49.880 --> 00:00:55.440
Laptop: Choose your vault and pick where to keep it. Okilum suggests a new, empty folder.

11
00:00:55.590 --> 00:00:58.500
Laptop: Your notes arrive, and the vault opens.

12
00:00:58.650 --> 00:01:03.170
Laptop: Write something on the laptop,

13
00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:06.170
Desktop: and it shows up on the desktop.

14
00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:09.840
Desktop: Change a note on the desktop,

15
00:01:09.990 --> 00:01:17.450
Laptop: and the laptop gets it too. You pair your computers once. After that, every change syncs both ways.
